Subject: [P23] winedmo: deliver read-ahead data errors when playback reaches them

With network read-ahead, a demux/bitstream-filter data error on a future
packet was queued as MEError immediately, ending playback seconds early and
discarding the queued good samples. Queue a payload-less error marker behind
the read-ahead data of every active stream and idle the demux thread; raise
the error when a stream dequeues the marker. Only STATUS_DATA_ERROR is
deferred; timeouts, disconnects, cancellation, shutdown and EOS are unchanged.
Seek/start clears the deferred state with the existing demux_eof reset.

